// ODDLY TRUE v2 · 1:30–2:00 · opening = the story itself, three turns, slowed climax, ending with meaning. One sentence = one shot.
// Bespoke act x3_cook (engine/library/bank/cook-under-the-sea.js); generic figures, no likeness.
# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=open cam=EWS.high.drop tail=.25
In May 2013, a ship's cook spent almost three days at the bottom of the sea… and lived.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=cabin nom=1 cam=WS.eye.push lead=.05 tail=.2
He was trapped inside an upside-down tugboat, thirty metres down, breathing from one bubble of air.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=waterline cam=MS.low.trackL lead=.05 tail=.35
This is how Harrison Okene made it out.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=night cam=WS.low.push lead=.05 tail=.15
It was about five in the morning, twenty miles off the coast of Nigeria.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=flip cam=MS.eye.handheld lead=.05 tail=.15 sfx="0.6:battle_creak:0.7"
Okene, the ship's cook, was on the toilet when the tugboat rolled over.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=sink cam=EWS.high.crane lead=.05 tail=.15 sfx="1.9:hit_sub_drop:0.6"
Water rushed in, and the boat sank upside down to the seabed.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=upside cam=MS.low.push lead=.05 tail=.25
The toilet was now on the ceiling.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=corridor cam=MCU.eye.trackL lead=.05 tail=.15
In total darkness, he felt his way along a flooded corridor in his underwear.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=surface cam=CU.low.static lead=.05 tail=.15
In an engineer's cabin, his head broke into a pocket of trapped air.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=cabin cam=WS.eye.orbit lead=.05 tail=.15
A bubble just over a metre high, under the upside-down floor.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=wreck cam=EWS.eye.push lead=.05 tail=.35
Of the twelve men on board, eleven never made it out.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=vest cam=CU.high.push lead=.05 tail=.15
In the black water, he found a life vest with two small torches… and a Coke.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=rise cam=MS.low.static lead=.05 tail=.15
But the bubble had a problem: the water was cold, and it was rising.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=air cam=WS.high.push lead=.05 tail=.15
A physicist later worked out that the bubble held about sixty hours of air.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=can cam=ECU.high.push lead=.05 tail=.15
He was so thirsty, he said, the salt water took the skin off his tongue.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=eyes cam=ECU.eye.static lead=.05 tail=.3
He prayed for one thing: to see some kind of light.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=eyes2 cam=CU.eye.static lead=.05 tail=.3
One day passed. Then a second.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=divers cam=WS.high.crane lead=.05 tail=.15
On the third day, a team of divers came down, sent to recover the bodies.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=pass cam=MS.eye.orbit lead=.05 tail=.45
The first diver swam right past him.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=hand cam=CU.eye.push lead=.05 tail=.2
Okene reached into the light and grabbed the second diver's hand.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=alive cam=MCU.ots.static lead=.05 tail=.55
"He's alive! He's alive!"

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=bell cam=WS.low.crane lead=.05 tail=.3
He rose in a diving bell, then spent three days in a decompression chamber.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=career cam=MS.eye.drop lead=.05 tail=.3
Two years later, he went back under the sea… as a qualified commercial diver.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=lamp cam=CU.eye.push lead=.1 tail=.8
The man who waited in the dark for a diver's light now carries one.
